From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] toplevel: Keep a floating autohide panel up over its gap

The gap between a floating panel and its edge belongs to no surface, so a
pointer going there left the panel, which hid. That left the pointer on the
hidden panel's strip, which showed it again, and so on. Revealing the panel at
the screen's last row of pixels ended the same way.

Keep the autohide strip, an input-only surface that already counts as the panel
and reserves nothing, mapped over the gap while the panel is shown. It takes the
clicks in the gap along the panel's length. A panel that isn't floating maps no
strip while shown, as before.
---
 mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c b/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c
--- a/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c
+++ b/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c
@@ -5066,12 +5066,18 @@
 	GdkRectangle *g;
 	int          auto_hide_size;
 	int          hit_size;
+	int          floating_margin;
 
 	if (!toplevel->priv->autohide_window)
 		return;
 
+	/* While a floating panel is shown the surface covers its gap to the
+	 * edge, so that a pointer there is still on the panel. */
+	floating_margin = panel_toplevel_get_floating_margin (toplevel);
+
 	if (!toplevel->priv->auto_hide ||
-	    toplevel->priv->state != PANEL_STATE_AUTO_HIDDEN ||
+	    (toplevel->priv->state != PANEL_STATE_AUTO_HIDDEN &&
+	     (toplevel->priv->state != PANEL_STATE_NORMAL || floating_margin == 0)) ||
 	    toplevel->priv->geometry.width <= 0 ||
 	    toplevel->priv->geometry.height <= 0) {
 		/* reset the cache so a later show (possibly at the same
@@ -5094,7 +5100,8 @@
 	 * pixel to unhide the panel. */
 	panel_toplevel_get_monitor_geometry (toplevel, &monitor_geom);
 	auto_hide_size = panel_toplevel_get_effective_auto_hide_size (toplevel);
-	hit_size = auto_hide_size + AUTO_HIDE_HIT_MARGIN;
+	hit_size = toplevel->priv->state == PANEL_STATE_NORMAL ?
+		   floating_margin : auto_hide_size + AUTO_HIDE_HIT_MARGIN;
 
 	g = &new_g;
 
@@ -5836,6 +5843,8 @@
 		gtk_widget_queue_draw (GTK_WIDGET (toplevel));
 	}
 
+	panel_toplevel_update_autohide_window (toplevel);
+
 	g_object_notify (G_OBJECT (toplevel), "floating");
 }
 
